Subject: btree_gist: drop an fmgr record with no function
Last-Update: 2026-09-29

btree_gist declares a version-1 info record for gbt_timetz_sortsupport,
which no source file defines and nothing looks up. A linked-in module's
table of entry points is generated from its archive and needs the
function beside every record, so drop the record.

diff --git a/contrib/btree_gist/btree_time.c b/contrib/btree_gist/btree_time.c
index 1dba950..d8607f2 100644
--- a/contrib/btree_gist/btree_time.c
+++ b/contrib/btree_gist/btree_time.c
@@ -28,7 +28,6 @@ PG_FUNCTION_INFO_V1(gbt_timetz_consistent);
 PG_FUNCTION_INFO_V1(gbt_time_penalty);
 PG_FUNCTION_INFO_V1(gbt_time_same);
 PG_FUNCTION_INFO_V1(gbt_time_sortsupport);
-PG_FUNCTION_INFO_V1(gbt_timetz_sortsupport);
 
 
 #ifdef USE_FLOAT8_BYVAL
